  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will develop methods to identify and isolate Short Tandem Repeat (STR) markers specifically for forest elephants in order to better determine whether there are evolutionarily distinct subpopulations of forest elephants within the Congo Basin, and whether these evolutionary patterns could be used to more accurately determine the site of origin of elephant specimens (like ivory). Specific activities will include a) development of STR markers from forest elephant samples, b) genotyping at least 110 forest elephant samples from six locations (Sierra Leone, Lope, Odzala, Dzanga-Sangha, Bili and Garamba) and comparing those to savanna elephant samples, c) analyzing the genotypes to determine whether samples from different forest sites can be accurately distinguished.</narrative>
  </description>
